Day 63 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

- Problem: 129. Sum Root to Leaf Numbers
- Approach:
I used DFS + Recursion to build the number represented by each root-to-leaf path.
Start with path = 0.
At every node, update the current number using:
 path = path × 10 + node.val
When a leaf node is reached, add the constructed number to the total sum.
Recursively explore both the left and right subtrees.

-Time Complexity :O(N)
-Space Complexity: O(H)

- Key Takeaways:
1) Practiced DFS on Binary Trees
2) Learned how to carry information through recursive calls
3) Understood how root-to-leaf paths can be converted into numbers
